Track 2: S-VHS Trapped in the Spindle
- Story & Context: Inside an abandoned broadcast relay booth overlooking the sunken harbor, Thorne watched water levels rise against the glass while feeding salvaged magnetic tape into a dying deck that chewed every spool it touched. Chen leaned against the doorframe, circular-breathing a single low B-flat until the glass vibrated, matching Thorne’s dead-eyed confession: "I traded your cassette for a canister of clean fuel." The track caught the exact moment the spindle jammed, turning the tape stretch into an accidental rhythmic thud that became the foundation of their live set.
