Track 3: Who Left the DAT Deck Running?
- Story & Context: The morning after the maritime security raided the high-line docks, divers found a master DAT recorder still spinning in an airtight pelican case tethered to an antenna mast. The tape had captured three hours of receding storm winds, distant siren groans, and Chen’s final low-register trill repeating like a mechanical foghorn while Thorne murmured into the dead channel, "The sound stays breathing long after the dock goes under." That salvaged digital tape was duplicated hand-to-hand across fifty survival flotillas, turning an abandoned rehearsal into the scene’s founding relic.
